\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK: Nikkei Off 0.1%; China Data Fails To Impress\b0\par\par\uc2 1,718 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Oktober 2010\par 06:37\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in Singapore. 65 64154 140; \par MarketTalk@dowjones.com \par  \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 0437 GMT [Dow Jones] Nikkei down 0.1% at 9370.32, falling back into negative territory after posting 0.2% gain in morning session. Investors remain nervous about stronger yen trend (USD/JPY now 81.14 vs intraday high of 81.84) and amid absence of positive surprise from slew of key economic data from China (3Q GDP +9.6% vs economists' expectations of +9.5%). "With the United States expected to continue monetary easing measures for some time, it's unlikely the weaker dollar trend will change in the next 6 months to a year," says Yoshinori Nagano, senior strategist at \uc2 Daiwa Asset Management\uc2 , though noting possibility of short-term technical rebound in USD/JPY. Puts near-term support lines for Nikkei at 9360 and 9200. 24/33 Topix subindexes lower; \uc2 Central Japan Railway\uc2  (9022.TO), or "JR Central", down 6.2% at Y606,000 on concerns over funds needed to build magnetic levitation train line connecting Tokyo and Nagoya. Select exporters off; \uc2 Ricoh\uc2  (7752.TO) down 1.9% at Y1,196 and Canon (7751.TO) down 0.8% at Y3,730. \uc2 Oji Paper\uc2  (3861.TO) up 0.8% at Y372 on Nikkei report of solid outlook for April-September earnings.(kana.inagaki@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0432 GMT [Dow Jones] MOF sells Y999.8 billion of 1.8% 20-year bonds with lowest price of 100.40, yielding 1.772%; results tad stronger than market expectations. While bid-to-cover ratio deteriorates to 4.41 from 4.56 last tender, lowest tender price of 100.40 above expected 100.30, while tail much shorter at 0.04 vs 0.20. Auction results positive for now, but concerns remain about possible