\par\par \b \uc2 FACTBOX-Steps countries are taking to counter hot money\b0\par\par\uc2 698 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Oktober 2010\par 23:16\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  Oct 21 (Reuters) - More governments around the world are moving to keep their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  from appreciating as investors, turning their backs on low interest rates in developed economies, pour money into higher-yielding markets.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  tensions will be in focus for finance leaders at a Group of 20 rich and emerging nations meeting in South Korea later this week.\par \par \uc2  Below are recent cases of direct or indirect government \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, compiled by Reuters:\par \par \uc2  THAILAND TAXES FOREIGN BOND INVESTORS\par \par \uc2  * Thailand imposes 15 pct withholding tax on interest and capital gains earned by foreign investors on Thai bonds.\par \par \uc2  * Tax became effective Oct 13, 2010, applicable to bonds issued by government, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and state enterprises.\par \par \uc2  * The Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the baht, has risen 11 pct against the U.S. dollar this year to levels not seen since the 1997 Asian financial crisis.\par \par \uc2  -- Story links: [ID:nSGE69K03E] [ID:nSGE69B0A6]\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 JAPAN\b0 \highlight\uc2  CUTS RATES, \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENES\b0 \highlight\uc2  FOR FIRST TIME SINCE 2004\par \par \uc2  * Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  unexpectedly pledged to pump more funds into the economy on Oct 5 and launched "comprehensive monetary easing," cutting rates to virtually zero.\par \par \uc2  * Authorities \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Sept. 15, the first time since 2004, to drive down yen, selling an estimated 2 trillion yen. Figures later show September sales total 2.1249 trillion yen ($25.37 billion)\par \par \uc2  * Prime minister signals Tokyo ready to keep \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  * Finance minister says United States did not comment on \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  at meeting in Washington on Oct 9 [ID:nTOE69801I]\par \par \uc2  BRAZIL TAKES MORE AGGRESSIVE ACTION\par \par \uc2  * Brazil warns of "\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  war"\par \par \uc2  * Government raises tax on foreigners buying local bonds for second time since start of October\par \par \uc2  * Also raises derivatives tax\par \par \uc2  * Brazil sovereign fund yet to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  * \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  steps up daily dollar auctions\par \par \uc2  -- Story link: [ID:nN18280200]\par \par \uc2  CHILE WARNS ON PESO, NO \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  YET\par \par \uc2  * President says worried but no plans for capital controls\par \par \uc2  * \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  slows pace of rate hikes, citing peso\par \par \uc2  * \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief says weighing \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  * Government to cut red tape to help exporters hit by peso\par \par \uc2  -- Story link: [ID:nN21292275] [ID:nN20242719]\par \par \uc2  SOUTH KOREA WARNS OF NEW LIMITS\par \par \uc2  * Regulator warns of further measures on forwards, asks banks not to lend in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  * \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  says will take new steps if foreign debt grows too fast\par \par \uc2  * Authorities repeatedly spotted buying dollars to curb the pace of appreciation in the won\par \par \uc2  * \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves rose more than $4 billion in September to a record level of $290 billion\par \par \uc2  -- Story links: [ID:nTOE69401M] [ID:nTOE697020] [ID:nTOE690069] [ID:nTOE69H00M]\par \par \uc2  INDIA \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENES\b0 \highlight\uc2  FOR FIRST TIME THIS YEAR\par \par \uc2  * Indian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought dollars for the first time this year, according to traders.\par \par \uc2  -- Story link: [ID:nSGE69D0EX]\par \par \uc2  PHILIPPINES MAY RELAX \b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  RULES IN RESPONSE TO INFLOWS\par \par \uc2  * \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  says considering relaxing \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rules to cope with huge inflows\par \par \uc2  * Bank to stay active in market as peso rises\par \par \uc2  Story link [ID:nSGE6950ES] [ID:nSGE69G01N]\par \par \uc2  INDONESIA \b \highlight22\uc2 CENTRAL BANK\b0 \highlight\uc2  WIDENS RANGE OF MATURITIES\par \par \uc2  * Finance minister says expects stable rupiah\par \par \uc2  * \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  says unworried about capital inflows, will try to manage rupiah \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  * \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  introduced a minimum holding period for its bills in June by offering a wider range of maturities\par \par \uc2  * Investors must hold the bills for minimum of one month\par \par \uc2  -- Story links [ID:nJAK423860] [ID:nJAK536689] [ID:nSGE65F0BV] [ID:nWAT014685]\par \par \uc2  COLOMBIA MULLS OFF-SHORE TAX PAYMENTS, CENBANK \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENES\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  * \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  makes it easier to control peso in market\par \par \uc2  * Government may allow multinationals to pay tax offshore\par \par \uc2  * \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  buying at least $20 million daily\par \par \uc2  * Analysts say move insufficient, other measures expected\par \par \uc2  -- Story link: [ID:nN15204150]\par \par \uc2  PERU PLANS TO LIMIT \b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  FORWARDS, EASES FUND OUTFLOWS\par \par \uc2  * Cenbank orders new rise in minimum deposit requirements\par \par \uc2  * Banking regulator eyes limits on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  forwards\par \par \uc2  * Rates on hold, possibly easing pressure on sol\par \par \uc2  * Pension funds allowed to hold more assets abroad\par \par \uc2  * \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading near two-year high against dollar\par \par \uc2  * Peru's sol to be boosted by 6-7 pct growth in 2011\par \par \uc2  -- Story links: [ID:nN21106328]\par \par \uc2  MEXICO SAYS NO PLANS FOR CAPITAL CONTROLS\par \par \uc2  * Finance minister says restrictions won't work\par \par \uc2  -- Story link: [ID:nWBT014190]    \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2 /CONTROLS (FACTBOX)|LANGEN|Table|ABN|D|E|RBN|M|U|RNP|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020101021e6al001xh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
