\par\par \b \uc2 =DJ  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2  VIEW: Speculative Bets Suggest Dollar Could Extend Rebound\b0\par\par\uc2 790 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Oktober 2010\par 04:39\par \uc2 Dow Jones Chinese Financial Wire\par \uc2 DJCFWE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2010, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 By Don Curren\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    A DOW JONES NEWSWIRES COLUMN\par \par   The dollar may have fallen so far out of favor that the only place for it to go is up.\par \par   The net short position, or negative bet, against the U.S. dollar among speculative traders remained at markedly high levels in the week that ended last Tuesday, suggesting the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  could continue to rebound as markets fine tune their expectations for further monetary stimulus from the Federal Reserve.\par \par   In this case, the data suggest speculators have gone as far as they are comfortable with in selling off the dollar on expectations the Federal Reserve will provide further monetary stimulus to the U.S. economy through quantitative easing. In quantitative easing, a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  creates new money to buy government bonds or other securities. The policy is considered corrosive for \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  since it increases the money supply and signals continued low interest rates.\par \par   The fact the collective bet against the dollar appears to have peaked indicates the U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  could rebound, said \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  analysts at \f28 \uc2 \f2 UBS\f28 \uc2 \f2 . "[With] positioning so extreme for a second successive week, a dollar rebound looks imminent," they said in a report.\par \par   The net overall speculative bet against the dollar was at $33.8 billion last Tuesday, according to data that the Commodities Futures Trading Commission in the U.S. released Friday.\par \par   That's high, but down slightly from last week and still below the $36.2 billion level record from November 2007, according to \f28 \uc2 \f2 TD Securities\f28 \uc2 \f2 . At the very least, the large size of the current anti-dollar position will tend to inhibit traders from piling on more bets against the dollar.\par \par    "The positioning is so extended, in aggregate, that...anyone who is even a trend-follower is asking themselves questions regarding the prudence of continuing on in the trend," said Sacha Tihanyi, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist at Scotia Capital.\par \par   The greenback has in fact already recovered to some extent since a speech on Friday by Fed Chairman Ben Bernanke had market participants reconsidering the extent of quantitative easing. Any corresponding changes in speculative positioning won't be known until the report for the week ending Oct. 19 becomes available Friday. The speculative position data from the Commodities Futures Trading Commission reflect only a small portion of overall \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market flows, but provide insight into broader movements in the market.\par \par   Bets for and against other major \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  also remained fairly stable in the week covered by the report from the previous week. The largest change was a decrease in the net positive bet on the euro to 42,000 contracts, the equivalent of C$7.2 billion, from 48,000 the previous week.\par \par   The lack of adjustment in overall positioning reflects "how well the Federal Reserve has conditioned the market to expect a major policy shift" at the end of its two-day policy meeting on Nov. 3, \f28 \uc2 \f2 UBS\f28 \uc2 \f2  said. "Investors have simply positioned in advance and now remain in wait-and-see mode," it said.\par \par   "[Looking] beyond the dollar, the steadiness of positioning elsewhere demonstrates how dominant the Fed's [quantitative easing] theme has been," \f28 \uc2 \f2 UBS\f28 \uc2 \f2  said. "Local developments in other \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  during the past week (and there were many) are clearly now a matter of secondary importance."\par \par   The data also reflect a substantial continued bet in favor of the yen, totaling about $7.4 billion, despite the market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  against the yen in September by Japanese officials concerned about the impact of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strength on the economy.\par \par   The longer Japan stays out of the market, the more aggressive bets in favor of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will tend to be, said Scotia's Tihanyi. "I think it's basically saying the longer the Japanese defer from \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  again, the braver people will get," he said.\par \par   Market players are likely conjecturing that political pressure against \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will tie \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's hands in the short term, and that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will hold off on any further \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  until the meeting of the Group of 20 advancing and emerging economies this weekend, he added.\par \par   (Don Curren, a reporter based in Toronto, has covered Canadian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and fixed income markets for more than 10 years. He can be reached at 416-306-2020 or at don.curren@dowjones.com.)\par \par    (TALK BACK: We invite readers to send us comments on this or other financial news topics. Please email us at TalkbackAmericas@dowjones.com. Readers should include their full names, work or home addresses and telephone numbers for verification purposes. We reserve the right to edit and publish your comments along with your name; we reserve the right not to publish reader comments.)\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -0-\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Copyright (c) 2010 \f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones & Company, Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 . \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJCFWE0020101020e6aj002gx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
