\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK: Further  \highlight22\uc2 Japan Intervention \highlight\uc2  May Anger US -  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  Asia\b0\par\par\uc2 1,305 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Oktober 2010\par 10:27\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in Singapore. 65 64154 140; \par MarketTalk@dowjones.com \par  \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0827 GMT [Dow Jones] \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's avoidance of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  since last month may be partly due to worries that further action could add to Washington's frustrations. Though U.S. officials mostly quiet, they were unhappy about Tokyo's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  last month as it came at time when they were trying to persuade China to adopt market-oriented \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rates. This may require Japan to be cautious about acting again; should U.S. begin to openly grumble about Tokyo action, that could weaken impact of potential \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , as signs of policy split between two nations tend to embolden JPY-buying speculators. Also, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's September \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  apparently done without U.S. approval, source says; Tokyo lawmakers tried to show leadership to Japanese people irritated by government's inability to stop JPY rises. See \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Asia: Further \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan Intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Risks Washington's Ire. (takashi.nakamichi@dowjones.com )\f28 \par \par \uc2 0825 GMT [Dow Jones] EUR/\uc2 NOK\uc2  is set to rise further as support at 8.13