\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK: EUR/JPY Close To 110 Bear Move - Charting Europe\b0\par\par\uc2 1,281 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Oktober 2010\par 12:37\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par Markettalk.eu@dowjones.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1037 GMT [Dow Jones] With the Japanese yen continuing to strengthen, defying the threat of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  from the Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , the EUR/JPY is on the crest of a slippery slope as weakness is expected to the 110.00 area this week. See Monday's Charting Europe column by Francis Bray. (francis.bray@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 1032 GMT [Dow Jones] India's wholesale price index print for September, which was tad higher at 8.62% vs 8.55% estimated in Dow Jones poll, could pressure \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to implement 25 bp hike in both policy rates (key lending rate and borrowing rate) on Nov. 2, says \uc2 Barclays Capital\uc2  in note. Adds, RBI has already hiked rates by enough to temper expectations of further price rises as momentum of inflation was negative, while RBI officials have recently indicated policy rates are close to neutral. "However, given the RBI's preference for lower volatility in overnight rates, we do not rule out a further narrowing in the 'corridor.'" RBI has lifted key lending rate by 125 bps, key borrowing rate by 175 bps so far this year.(khushita.vasant@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1023 GMT [Dow Jones] \uc2 HSBC\uc2  doesn't expect Poland's monetary policy council to hike rates this year, but adds the next move would highly likely be upwards. "This, coupled with IMF's flexible credit line, argues for continued strength for the Polish zloty," the bank adds. Sees spot EUR/PLN at 3.90 at 4Q '10 end and has hold recommendation for PLN. (malgorzata.halaba@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1023 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/PKR at 86.10 late Monday, unchanged from Friday; "trading was light in the beginning of the week as importers sat out, expecting exporters could come in to sell," says a dealer. Notes, current high dollar levels look attractive for exporters to offload holdings. Tips pair in 86.05-86.10 range Tuesday amid thin volume. (djn.in@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1019 GMT [Dow Jones] Indonesia government bond prices edge lower on profit-taking after last week's rally. "It's a healthy correction after the rally," and will help keep concerns an asset-price bubble may be forming in check, trader at local brokerage firm says; adds "expect a rebound tomorrow as demand remain high." 5-year yield up at 6.38% vs 6.37% Friday; 10-year at 7.10% vs 7.07%; 15-year at 7.59% vs 7.57%; and 20-year steady at 7.95%. (andreasismar.sandiwan@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1018 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/CHF needs to breach resistance at 0.9642 to signal a change in its short-term trend to neutral, according to technical analysts at \uc2 Bank Sarasin\uc2 . "A break above 0.9731 will change the short-term trend to positive, while a break above 0.9918 will signal a medium-term neutral trend," they say. USD/CHF at 0.9616 by 1008 GMT. (neil.maclucas@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1011 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/INR forward premia tad lower, but well supported as higher exporter propensity to sell as spot drifts higher, matched by heavy paying in front-end contracts as foreign funds bringing USD in for \uc2 Coal India Ltd\uc2  IPO, buying back USD in forward market to hedge \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  risk for period of issue, says trader with foreign bank; 1-year forward premium at 2.34 vs 2.355 late Friday. "Premia are pretty firm with the foreign funds looking to pay the near-months in the offshore NDF contract, and that's boosting onshore premia as well," says trader. Tips premia to stay well supported, although some correction on cards once inflows fully hedged. (bijou.george@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1001 GMT [Dow Jones] Euro Overnight Index Average fixes higher Friday at 0.745% vs Thursday's 0.742%. Monday, the interbank overnight rate is trading in a wider range between 0.70% and 0.80% from 0.70% and 0.75% Friday. A money trader says this is a relatively high level. Adds he expects liquidity to recede somewhat due to the start of the minimum reserve requirement period. Earlier Monday, 3-month Euribor fixed at 1% vs 0.993% Friday. (thomas.leppert@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0957 GMT [Dow Jones] Room for further INR appreciation appears limited as short USD positions showing signs of being overstretched; also \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may join \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  bandwagon to hold down INR gains vs USD, says \uc2 Barclays Capital\uc2  in note. INR touched fresh over 25-month high of 43.97 vs greenback Friday. House says, \uc2 Coal India Ltd\uc2 .'s up to $3.5 billion share sale, which opened for subscription Monday, will be highly oversubscribed but could see some foreign fund repatriation once IPO allocation is finalized. "In the medium term, we think the rising current account deficit and weaker fundamentals are likely to result in INR underperforming against other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ." Tips USD/INR to trade in 43.90-44.50 band in week. Recommends buy in 1-month USD/INR ATMF put. Pair last at 44.27 vs 44.12 late Friday.(khushita.vasant@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0947 GMT [Dow Jones] Thai shares end down 1.3% at 984.03 in active trade, with losses accelerating mid-afternoon, led by PTT group shares after recent run-up, while banks also slipping ahead of 3Q earnings due this week. Selldown comes after market again failed to breach 1000 point level last week, which last seen in November 1996. "Generally, it's just a little bit high. We've had very good run already, so dare I say it, there's some profit-taking," says Kenric Singhakowin from Asia Plus Securities. Support at 980, then 975, resistance at 990. Among most active, PTT (PTT.TH) down 1.6% at THB308, \uc2 PTT Aromatics and Refining\uc2  (PTTAR.TH) down 4.9% at THB29.25, \uc2 PTT Exploration & Production\uc2  (PTTEP.TH) down 2.9% at THB169, \uc2 Charoen Pokphand Foods\uc2  (CPF.TH) down 3% at THB23, \uc2 Krung Thai Bank\uc2  (KTB.TH) down 4% at THB17, Bangkok Bank (BBL.TH) down 1.9% at THB155.50, \uc2 Kasikornbank\uc2  (KBANK.TH) down 0.9% at THB116.50. (leigh.murray@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0946 GMT [Dow Jones] Spain's 15-year bond offer Thursday will be a good indicator of the extent of renewed investor confidence in higher yielding euro sovereigns, says Credit Agricole CIB. Spain, which will announce the auction's target volume later Monday, will also auction a non-benchmark bond at primary dealers' request. The bonds on auction Thursday are the 4.65% July 2025 and 5.75% July 2032. (emese.bartha@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0943 GMT [Dow Jones] Sensex flat at 20,118.64, rebounds after touching day's low 19,870.51 (below 20,000 mark 1st time since Sep. 30) on short-covering, says local dealer. "Investors are booking profits to invest in \uc2 Coal India\uc2 's $3.43 billion share sale," says \uc2 Anand Rathi Financial Services\uc2 ' DD Sharma; Sensex +12% since Sept. 1. Sharma says markets will bounce back after \uc2 Coal India\uc2  IPO closes Oct. 21; tips 20,200-19,500 range, support at 19,100 for today. \uc2 Larsen & Toubro\uc2  (500510.BY) flat at INR1,990.75, \uc2 Housing Development Finance Corp\uc2 . (500010.BY) down 1% at INR719.50, both off lows after 2Q earnings above analysts' forecasts. TCS (532540.BY) +2.7% at INR976.40, \uc2 Bharti Airtel\uc2 (532454.BY) down 2.1% at INR327.15, ACC(500410.BY) off 2.9% at INR970 (suhita.poddar@dowjones.com) [ 10-18-10 0637ET ]\par \par \uc2 4022   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020101018e6ai0006j\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
