\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK: USD/JPY Vols Tad Higher As Spot Edges Down\b0\par\par\uc2 1,519 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Oktober 2010\par 05:25\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in Singapore. 65 64154 140; \par MarketTalk@dowjones.com \par  \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0325 GMT [Dow Jones] Volatilities implied by 1-month ATM USD/JPY options edge up 11.70%/12.40% from 11.60%/12.30% Friday in NY as demand increases for hedges vs further spot falls. USD/JPY last 81.36 after dropping to 80.95 earlier, vs 81.41 in late Friday. Rise in vols also comes as some investors interested in purchasing short-term upside hedges in expectation of JPY-selling \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by Tokyo, says senior dealer at major brokerage in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . But adds vols unlikely to change much from current levels in coming sessions as players likely to be in "wait-and-see mode" ahead of widely anticipated G-20 meeting later this week. (kosaku.narioka@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 0323 GMT [Dow Jones] NZD/USD trending lower due to increased risk aversion globally, says \uc2 RBC Capital Markets\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist Sue Trinh; "The third quarter CPI has had little bearing on the price action as Kiwi has been dragged lower by the risk off move, led by euro and what appears to be increasing concerns" about Portugal; Portuguese Finance Minister Fernando Teixeira dos Santos warned in interview with SIC Noticias TV on Sunday that government would be shut out of international bond markets, would have to seek external help if its 2011 budget were to be rejected; pair last 0.7516 vs 0.7564 early. Adds there's further downside risk overnight as recent "rally in risk occurred with very little in the way of a meaningful pullback." Says market will be watching U.S. housing data overnight, plus earnings from \uc2 Citigroup\uc2 . Tips support at 0.7480 with resistance at 0.7550. (lucy.craymer@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0322 GMT [Dow Jones] Aussie name bought good amounts of USD/SGD from 1.3010 this morning, driving pair as high as 1.3050, purportedly executing an AUD/SGD order, says Singapore-based dealer. USD/SGD last quoted in interbank market at 1.3031-1.3036. (jerry.tan@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0319 GMT [Dow Jones] Thai shares down 0.3% at 994.59 in light trade, tracking regional stocks, with some PTT (PTT.TH) group shares easing after solid gains last week while some banks also coming under pressure ahead of 3Q earnings reports this week, also expected decision by BOT to keep rates steady Wednesday, says \uc2 Kim Eng Securities\uc2  strategist Mayuree Chowvikran. Support pegged at 990, resistance at 1000. Among top actives, PTT down 0.3% at THB312, \uc2 PTT Aromatics and Refining\uc2  (PTTAR.TH) down 0.8% at THB30.50, \uc2 PTT Exploration and Production\uc2  (PTTEP.TH) down 1.4% at THB171.50, Bangkok Bank (BBL.TH) down 0.6% at THB157.50, \uc2 Krung Thai Bank\uc2  (KTB.TH) down 0.6% at THB17.60, \uc2 Siam Commercial Bank\uc2  (SCB.TH) down 0.9% at THB106.50. (leigh.murray@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0318 GMT [Dow Jones] Vietnam shares last down 0.3% at 456.25 with local selling on concerns serious floods in the central region will disrupt \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  of many companies as north-south transportation activities cut off for some days. "In addition to concerns about high interest rates, bad news about flooding and stormy conditions in the central region are also discouraging players from buying stocks now," says trader. Adds, buying appetite also remains weak because 3Q results still awaited as companies slow in releasing them. Volume thin with 11 million shares valued at VND290 billion traded. Among decliners, \uc2 BaoViet Holdings\uc2  (BVH.VH) down 2.3% at VND63,000, Ocean Group (OGC.VH) down 1.4% at VND53,000, Vietcombank (VCB.VH) down 1.1% at VND36,000. Trader tips immediate support for key index at 455. (phammuoi.nguyen@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0311 GMT [Dow Jones] Thai government bonds higher in lackluster trade. Yields expected to inch lower as foreign fund inflows likely to continue amid bearish view toward USD, says local dealer. Adds, players reluctant to aggressively build up positions ahead of \uc2 Bank of Thailand\uc2 's rate decision Wednesday. Among 12 economists surveyed by Dow Jones, 10 forecast \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stand pat, keeping policy rate unchanged at 1.75%, while two expect 25 bps hike. Bid/offer yields of issue due December 2015 quoted at 2.43%/2.39% vs 2.44%/2.40% late Friday, November 2016 at 2.57%/2.50% vs 2.58%/2.55%, June 2019 at 2.77%/2.70% vs 2.81%/2.78%. (piyarat.setthasiriphaiboon@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0310 GMT [Dow Jones] Indian government bonds likely down as firm inflation print Friday likely to keep market jittery, stoke rate hike talk ahead of RBI's November 2 policy meeting, says trader with foreign bank; tips 7.80% 2020 government bond to open at around 98.10 vs 98.24 last close, but find support at 98.00. "It's getting close to the RBI policy meeting and with a high inflation print you'll find people a bit wary of buying too much into bonds," says trader. Notes market now likely to pencil in at least 25bp rate hike at policy meet if not more, given stubbornly high inflation. WPI inflation for September printed at 8.62% on year vs 8.55% estimate in Dow Jones poll. (bijou.george@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0308 GMT [Dow Jones] For investors with view that HSI's 2-day pullback just normal profit-taking, \uc2 Hutchison Whampoa\uc2 's (0013.HK) share-price performance maybe indicator to gauge when correction may be ending. Bellwether conglomerate led HSI's current round of rally, surged to HK$77.20 Oct. 8 (+34% vs Aug. 31 close), then started to correct ahead of HSI correction, with today's intraday low of HK$72.55 marking 6.0% correction from peak. Stock now rebounding from intraday low, last +0.5% at HK$74.40 -- could be signal broad market downdraft may be nearing end. HSI last down 1.1% at 23,504.25, off 23,482.61 low. (robert.li@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0302 GMT [Dow Jones] Korea government bonds, bond futures lower, tracking losses in U.S. Treasurys Friday, while foreigners sell futures. But market participants don't expect any steep losses, with shorter-end bonds outperforming on prevailing view BOK likely to keep policy rate at 2.25% for rest of this year. 2-year monetary stabilization bond yield +2 bps at 3.06%, 5-year government bond yield +4 bps at 3.49%, 10-year yield +5 bps at 3.97%, December futures down 10 ticks at 113.39. Bond manager at local securities firm tips futures in 113.30-113.50 range; "if shorter-end bonds strengthen in the afternoon, it could give the longer-end bonds a leg up as well." (min-jeong.lee@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0258 GMT [Dow Jones] \uc2 Bank of Thailand\uc2  likely to shrug off mounting concern over appreciating THB vs USD and lift benchmark policy rate 25 bps to 2.0% at Wednesday's meeting, says Tisco Securities. House says BOT's reiterated several times that process of rate normalization is underway, should continue to prevent economic imbalances arising; says \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has also contended that interest rate differential with overseas peers having minimal impact on THB. While THB's rapid rise to 13-year highs helping contain inflationary pressure, along with government's decision to extend subsidy program for low-income earnings until year-end, "nonetheless, we see a potential upside risk for consumer prices due to cost pass-through effects as the economy gains momentum, with the main impact expected to be felt next year." (leigh.murray@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0253 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/INR likely to open higher as broadly firm global USD likely to support, while likely weak local stocks to also lift pair, says trader with foreign bank; tips pair to open around 44.25 vs 44.12 late Friday, trade in 44.00-44.40 band in session. "We expect portfolio inflows targeted at the \uc2 Coal India\uc2  IPO to continue, but expect strong corporate demand at lower levels to help neutralise this," says trader. Foreign funds were net sellers of provisional INR1.13 billion worth of Indian shares Friday. (bijou.george@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0245 GMT [Dow Jones] Big unwind of USD short positions at start of trading continuing as Asia rolls on, weighing on AUD/USD in process, says Greg Gibbs, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategy RBS Australia. "The market went a long way on the QE story and Friday was a bit of a turning point on that. The markets in Asia are viewing that speech (from Fed Bernanke) and taking some profits on those short dollar trades." AUD/USD recently at 0.9846, falling from earlier highs around 0.9930 after hitting parity briefly early Friday in US. Looking to next 24 hours, lot of local focus will be on RBA minutes from October meetings when it shocked economists by keeping rates steady at 4.5%. (geoffrey.rogow@dowjones.com) [ 10-17-10 2325ET ]\par \par \uc2 4022   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020101018e6ai0002a\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
