\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 1,367 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Oktober 2010\par 10:01\par \uc2 Dow Jones Emerging Markets Report\par \uc2 EM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  FINANCE MINISTER CONTINUES \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  TALK \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's finance minister kept the possibility of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market on the table Friday, saying the government will take "decisive" steps if necessary, after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  touched a 15-year high of Y80.88 to the dollar overnight. (published 0125 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par JAPAN PM KAN: VERY CONCERNED ABOUT YEN'S CURRENT SITUATION \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's Prime Minister Naoto Kan said Friday he is "very concerned" about the yen's continued climb, after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  touched a 15-year high of Y80.88 to the dollar overnight. (published 0227 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BOJ GOVERNOR: READY TO TAKE APPROPRIATE POLICY STEPS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bank of Japan Gov. Masaaki Shirakawa said Friday that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is ready to take appropriate monetary policy measures amid downside risks to the domestic economy such as the rising yen and slowing overseas economies. (published 0048 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par S KOREA FIN MIN: \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCY\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  TENSIONS GROWING, SEE SIGNS OF PROTECTIONISM \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korea's Minister of Strategy and Finance Yoon Jeung-hyun said Friday that tensions among advanced and emerging economies over \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rates are growing, and may result in countries setting up trade barriers. (published 0200 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA FDI GROWTH REBOUNDS AFTER 2-MONTH SLOWDOWN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Growth in foreign direct investment in China picked up in September after two consecutive months of declines, indicating the world's second-largest economy remains an attractive investment destination, especially as countries' stimulus policies are keeping the global financial system flush with cash. (published 0541 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA SEPTEMBER PROPERTY PRICES UP 1ST TIME SINCE MAY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's property prices edged higher in September from August in their first month-on-month increase in four months, underscoring the government's continuing struggle to stabilize a soaring real-estate market that prompted another round of tightening at the end of last month. (published 0457 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par US SENATOR BAUCUS REPEATS CALL FOR FASTER YUAN APPRECIATION \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.S. Senator Max Baucus repeated a call for China to allow faster appreciation of the yuan after meetings with Chinese officials, according to a statement Friday, adding to pressure over the issue as U.S. mid-term elections loom in November. (published 0526 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA: AGAINST WTO RULES FOR US TO ADOPT DISCRIMINATORY POLICIES ON YUAN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China said Friday it will move ahead with the yuan exchange rate reform based on its own needs, adding it would be against the World Trade Organization's rules for the U.S. to adopt any discriminatory policies on Beijing's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  issue. (published 0311 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PBOC ZHOU: TO CONTINUE TO MANAGE YUAN EXCHANGE RATE BASED ON EXISTING TRADING BAND - REPORT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China will continue to manage the yuan's exchange rate based on the existing trading band to maintain the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's basic stability, People's Bank of China Gov. Zhou Xiaochuan wrote in an article in the PBOC-backed magazine China Finance on Friday. (published 0050 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA: PRESSURE ON EXPORTERS IF YUAN RISES OVER 3% VS DOLLAR THIS YEAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Chinese exporters would come under pressure if the yuan gains more than 3% against the U.S. dollar this year, Yao Jian, a spokesman for China's Ministry of Commerce, said Friday. (published 0351 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PBOC: CHINA FINANCIAL FIRMS TO ISSUE AT LEAST CNY10 BLN YUAN BONDS IN HK 2010 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Chinese financial institutions will issue at least CNY10 billion worth of yuan-denominated bonds in Hong Kong this year, a People's Bank of China official said Friday. (published 0350 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TURKEY MINISTER: CONSIDERING \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  POLICY, IN NO HURRY TO CHANGE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Turkish government and the country's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  are considering measures to stem the rapid rise of the lira, but are "not in a hurry" to change \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  policy soon, Turkey's economics minister Ali Babacan said Friday. (published 0759 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PORTUGAL GOVERNMENT TO PRESENT KEY '11 BUDGET TO PARLIAMENT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Portugal's government Friday afternoon will present its long-awaited 2011 austerity budget to parliament amid continued uncertainty over whether it will pass. (published 0741 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par AUSTRALIAN CONSUMERS MARK DOWN HOUSE PRICE GROWTH EXPECTATIONS-WESTPAC \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Expectations of house price gains over the next year in Australia softened in October, according to a survey by \f28 \uc2 \f2 Westpac\f28 \uc2 \f2  and the Melbourne Institute. (published 2357 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par STATE BANK OF INDIA CHAIRMAN: PLAN TO ISSUE MORE RETAIL BONDS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 State Bank of India\f28 \uc2 \f2 , the country's largest lender by assets, plans to issue retail bonds on a frequent basis to fund its capital requirements, its chairman said Friday. (published 0723 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par INDIA SEPTEMBER WHOLESALE PRICE INDEX UP 8.62% ON YEAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 India's wholesale inflation rate accelerated to 8.62% in September from 8.51% in August, the government said Friday. (published 0625 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par MALAYSIA FORECASTS GDP GROWTH 7.0% IN 2010, 5%-6% IN 2011 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Malaysia has revised up its economic growth forecast for this year to 7.0%, as expected, but said the rate of expansion will probably slow to between 5.0% and 6.0% in 2011. (published 0800 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par MALAYSIA GOVERNMENT BORROWINGS LIKELY MYR65B IN 2010 VS MYR94B IN 2009 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Malaysia's total borrowings for 2010 is expected to decline to MYR65 billion, from MYR94 billion in 2009, because of lower loan repayments, redemptions and deficit financing requirements, the government said Friday in its annual report on the economy. (published 0800 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PHILIPPINE \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CENTRAL BANK\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 : MONETARY POLICY STILL APPROPRIATE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Bangko Sentral ng Pilipinas believes its current policy stance remains appropriate given the benign inflation outlook, but it is closely watching the impact of increasing capital inflows on asset prices. (published 0155 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PHILIPPINE BUDGET CHIEF HOPEFUL OF CREDIT RATING IMPROVEMENT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Philippine Budget Secretary Florencio Abad said Friday he is hopeful the upcoming review of economic and fiscal developments in the country by the three major international credit rating agencies will yield favorable results for one of Asia's most aggressive sovereign borrowers. (published 0322 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CZECH PPI ACCELERATES TO +2.4% ON YEAR IN SEPTEMBER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Czech industrial producer prices rose 2.4% on the year in September, accelerating from the 1.8% annual rise in August and overshooting market expectations, data released Friday by the Czech Statistics Office, or CSU, showed. (published 0701 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par THAI \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CENTRAL BANK\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  UNLIKELY TO USE FIXED EXCHANGE RATE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Thailand is unlikely to use a fixed exchange rate regime in a bid to stem the baht's sharp rise against the dollar, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Thailand\f28 \uc2 \f2  Governor Prasarn Trairatvorakul said Friday. (published 0541 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par THAI \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CENTRAL BANK\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  CHAIRMAN: NECESSITY TO HIKE RATE HAS BEEN REDUCED \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The need for the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Thailand\f28 \uc2 \f2  to raise its benchmark interest rate has been reduced, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's board chairman, Chatu Mongol Sonakul, said Friday. (published 0413 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     ======= DOW JONES NEWSWIRES ANALYSIS AND COMMENTARY ======= \par  \par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  FOCUS: TIME FOR THE FED TO SPELL IT OUT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Federal Reserve has been dangling the prospect of further quantitative easing in front of financial markets for months now, but after the fall in the dollar, it is not going to be enough to boost investor confidence. (published 0715 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par EUROPEAN \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  TECHNICALS: USD STAGING CORRECTIVE RECOVERY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Intraday EUR/USD: downside consolidation is underway off Thursday's eight-month high at 1.4123, but corrective weakness is expected to be limited to the 1.3995 area. While 1.3995 holds, a test of resistance at 1.4088 and the lower peak at 1.4110 is expected, but only movement above 1.4110 would re-open the 1.4123 high. There are signs that the short-term uptrend has over-stretched and a break below 1.3995 would upgrade the setback, exposing Wednesday's low at 1.3912. (published 0605 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par EUROPEAN INTEREST RATE TECHNICALS: BONDS TO WEAKEN FURTHER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Intraday BUND: Bears are back in control of the near term following Thursday's sharp setback, and more weakness is expected to put the Oct. 1 reaction low at 130.63 at risk. Tuesday's bull trap high at 132.36 dominates the near-term, and a sustained break below 130.63 would create room for an extension lower towards the 130.00 level. Only above projected resistance at 131.61 would negate the bearish outlook, which is protected by the 131.53 high. (published 0720 GMT) [ 15-10-10 0801GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1030 1804 4180   \par \par \uc2 Dokument EM00000020101015e6af0000k\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
