nd Finance Yoon Jeung-hyun said Friday that tensions among advanced and emerging economies over \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rates are growing, and may result in countries setting up trade barriers. (published 0200 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =UPDATE: CHINA FDI GROWTH REBOUNDS AFTER 2-MONTH SLOWDOWN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Growth in foreign direct investment in China picked up in September after two consecutive months of declines, indicating the world's second-largest economy remains an attractive investment destination, especially as countries' stimulus policies are keeping the global financial system flush with cash. (published 0541 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =UPDATE: CHINA SEPTEMBER PROPERTY PRICES UP 1ST TIME SINCE MAY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's property prices edged higher in September from August in their first month-on-month increase in four months, underscoring the government's continuing struggle to stabilize a soaring real-estate market that prompted another round of tightening at the end of last month. (published 0457 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par US SENATOR BAUCUS REPEATS CALL FOR FASTER YUAN APPRECIATION \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.S. Senator Max Baucus repeated a call for China to allow faster appreciation of the yuan after meetings with Chinese officials, according to a statement Friday, adding to pressure over the issue as U.S. mid-term elections loom in November. (published 0526 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par CHINA: AGAINST WTO RULES FOR US TO ADOPT DISCRIMINATORY POLICIES ON YUAN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China said Friday it will move ahead with the yuan exchange rate reform based on its own needs, adding it would be against the World Trade Organization's rules for the U.S. to adopt any discriminatory policies on Beijing's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  issue. (published 0311 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par PBOC ZHOU: TO CONTINUE TO MANAGE YUAN EXCHANGE RATE BASED ON EXISTING TRADING BAND - REPORT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China will continue to manage the yuan's exchange rate based on the existing trading band to maintain the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's basic stability, People's Bank of China Gov. Zhou Xiaochuan wrote in an article in the PBOC-backed magazine China Finance on Friday. (published 0050 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par CHINA: PRESSURE ON EXPORTERS IF YUAN RISES OVER 3% VS DOLLAR THIS YEAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Chinese exporters would come under pressure if the yuan gains more than 3% against the U.S. dollar this year, Yao Jian, a spokesman for China's Ministry of Commerce, said Friday. (published 0351 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par PBOC: CHINA FINANCIAL FIRMS TO ISSUE AT LEAST CNY10 BLN YUAN BONDS IN HK 2010 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Chinese financial institutions will issue at least CNY10 billion worth of yuan-denominated bonds in Hong Kong this year, a People's Bank of China official said Friday. (published 0350 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par AUSTRALIAN CONSUMERS MARK DOWN HOUSE PRICE GROWTH EXPECTATIONS-WESTPAC \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Expectations of house price gains over the next year in Australia softened in October, according to a survey by \f28 \uc2 \f2 Westpac\f28 \uc2 \f2  and the Melbourne Institute. (published 2357 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par PHILIPPINE \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CENTRAL BANK\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 : MONETARY POLICY STILL APPROPRIATE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Bangko Sentral ng Pilipinas believes its current policy stance remains appropriate given the benign inflation outlook, but it is closely watching the impact of increasing capital inflows on asset prices. (published 0155 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par PHILIPPINE BUDGET CHIEF HOPEFUL OF CREDIT RATING IMPROVEMENT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Philippine Budget Secretary Florencio Abad said Friday he is hopeful the upcoming review of economic and fiscal developments in the country by the three major international credit rating agencies will yield favorable results for one of Asia's most aggressive sovereign borrowers. (published 0322 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =2ND UPDATE: THAI \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CENTRAL BANK\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  UNLIKELY TO USE FIXED EXCHANGE RATE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Thailand is unlikely to use a fixed exchange rate regime in a bid to stem the baht's sharp rise against the dollar, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Thailand\f28 \uc2 \f2  Governor Prasarn Trairatvorakul said Friday. (published 0541 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par THAI \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CENTRAL BANK\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  CHAIRMAN: NECESSITY TO HIKE RATE HAS BEEN REDUCED \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The need for the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Thailand\f28 \uc2 \f2  to raise its benchmark interest rate has been reduced, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's board chairman, Chatu Mongol Sonakul, said Friday. (published 0413 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par THAI PM REITERATES 2010 GDP GROWTH FORECAST AROUND 8% \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Thailand's economy is forecast to expand by around 8% this year, Prime Minister Abhisit Vejjajiva reiterated Friday. (published 0301 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par RBNZ PROPOSES LIMITING BANKS' COVERED BOND ISSUANCE TO 10% OF TOTAL ASSETS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Reserve Bank of New Zealand Friday issued a consultation paper proposing to limit covered bond issuance by local financial institutions to 10% of their total assets and to develop a regulatory framework for covered bond programs. (published 0031 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =2ND UPDATE: FORTESCUE METALS READIES US$2B US/EUROPE BOND OFFER -SOURCES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australian iron-ore mining company \f28 \uc2 \f2 Fortescue Metals Group Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . is looking to raise US$2 billion in the U.S. and European bond markets, according to two people familiar with the matter, as the miner accelerates its expansion plans to capitalize on the currently high price of iron ore. (published 2327 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par CHINA RAILWAY GROUP TO SELL CNY6 BLN BONDS MONDAY-TUESDAY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China Railway Group Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., a state-owned builder of railway lines, said Friday it will sell CNY6 billion worth of bonds on the Shanghai Stock Exchange between Monday and Tuesday. (published 2345 GMT) [ 15-10-10 0602GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1030 1804 4180   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020101015e6af000cw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
