\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 1,115 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Oktober 2010\par 09:01\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  FINANCE MINISTER CONTINUES \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  TALK \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's finance minister kept the possibility of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market on the table Friday, saying the government will take "decisive" steps if necessary, after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  touched a 15-year high of Y80.88 to the dollar overnight. (published 0125 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par JAPAN PM KAN: VERY CONCERNED ABOUT YEN'S CURRENT SITUATION \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's Prime Minister Naoto Kan said Friday he is "very concerned" about the yen's continued climb, after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  touched a 15-year high of Y80.88 to the dollar overnight. (published 0227 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BOJ GOVERNOR: READY TO TAKE APPROPRIATE POLICY STEPS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bank of Japan Gov. Masaaki Shirakawa said Friday that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is ready to take appropriate monetary policy measures amid downside risks to the domestic economy such as the rising yen and slowing overseas economies. (published 0048 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par S KOREA FIN MIN: \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCY\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  TENSIONS GROWING, SEE SIGNS OF PROTECTIONISM \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korea's Minister of Strategy and Finance Yoon Jeung-hyun said Friday that tensions among advanced and emerging economies over \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rates are growing, and may result in countries setting up trade barriers. (published 0200 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA FDI GROWTH REBOUNDS AFTER 2-MONTH SLOWDOWN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Growth in foreign direct investment in China picked up in September after two consecutive months of declines, indicating the world's second-largest economy remains an attractive investment destination, especially as countries' stimulus policies are keeping the global financial system flush with cash. (published 0541 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA SEPTEMBER PROPERTY PRICES UP 1ST TIME SINCE MAY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's property prices edged higher in September from August in their first month-on-month increase in four months, underscoring the government's continuing struggle to stabilize a soaring real-estate market that prompted another round of tightening at the end of last month. (published 0457 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par US SENATOR BAUCUS REPEATS CALL FOR FASTER YUAN APPRECIATION \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.S. Senator Max Baucus repeated a call for China to allow faster appreciation of the yuan after meetings with Chinese officials, according to a statement Friday, adding to pressure over the issue as U.S. mid-term elections loom in November. (published 0526 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA: AGAINST WTO RULES FOR US TO ADOPT DISCRIMINATORY POLICIES ON YUAN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China said Friday it will move ahead with the yuan exchange rate reform based on its own needs, adding it would be against the World Trade Organization's rules for the U.S. to adopt any discriminatory policies on Beijing's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  issue. (published 0311 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PBOC ZHOU: TO CONTINUE TO MANAGE YUAN EXCHANGE RATE BASED ON EXISTING TRADING BAND - REPORT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China will continue to manage the yuan's exchange rate based on the existing trading band to maintain the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's basic stability, People's Bank of China Gov. Zhou Xiaochuan wrote in an article in the PBOC-backed magazine China Finance on Friday. (published 0050 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA: PRESSURE ON EXPORTERS IF YUAN RISES OVER 3% VS DOLLAR THIS YEAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Chinese exporters would come under pressure if the yuan gains more than 3% against the U.S. dollar this year, Yao Jian, a spokesman for China's Ministry of Commerce, said Friday. (published 0351 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PBOC: CHINA FINANCIAL FIRMS TO ISSUE AT LEAST CNY10 BLN YUAN BONDS IN HK 2010 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Chinese financial institutions will issue at least CNY10 billion worth of yuan-denominated bonds in Hong Kong this year, a People's Bank of China official said Friday. (published 0350 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par AUSTRALIAN CONSUMERS MARK DOWN HOUSE PRICE GROWTH EXPECTATIONS-WESTPAC \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Expectations of house price gains over the next year in Australia softened in October, according to a survey by \f28 \uc2 \f2 Westpac\f28 \uc2 \f2  and the Melbourne Institute. (published 2357 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par INDIA SEPTEMBER WHOLESALE PRICE INDEX UP 8.62% ON YEAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 India's wholesale inflation rate accelerated to 8.62% in September from 8.51% in August, the government said Friday. (published 0625 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PHILIPPINE \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CENTRAL BANK\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 : MONETARY POLICY STILL APPROPRIATE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Bangko Sentral ng Pilipinas believes its current policy stance remains appropriate given the benign inflation outlook, but it is closely watching the impact of increasing capital inflows on asset prices. (published 0155 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PHILIPPINE BUDGET CHIEF HOPEFUL OF CREDIT RATING IMPROVEMENT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Philippine Budget Secretary Florencio Abad said Friday he is hopeful the upcoming review of economic and fiscal developments in the country by the three major international credit rating agencies will yield favorable results for one of Asia's most aggressive sovereign borrowers. (published 0322 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par THAI \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CENTRAL BANK\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  UNLIKELY TO USE FIXED EXCHANGE RATE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Thailand is unlikely to use a fixed exchange rate regime in a bid to stem the baht's sharp rise against the dollar, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Thailand\f28 \uc2 \f2  Governor Prasarn Trairatvorakul said Friday. (published 0541 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par THAI \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CENTRAL BANK\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  CHAIRMAN: NECESSITY TO HIKE RATE HAS BEEN REDUCED \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The need for the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Thailand\f28 \uc2 \f2  to raise its benchmark interest rate has been reduced, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's board chairman, Chatu Mongol Sonakul, said Friday. (published 0413 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par THAI PM REITERATES 2010 GDP GROWTH FORECAST AROUND 8% \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Thailand's economy is forecast to expand by around 8% this year, Prime Minister Abhisit Vejjajiva reiterated Friday. (published 0301 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par RBNZ PROPOSES LIMITING BANKS' COVERED BOND ISSUANCE TO 10% OF TOTAL ASSETS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Reserve Bank of New Zealand Friday issued a consultation paper proposing to limit covered bond issuance by local financial institutions to 10% of their total assets and to develop a regulatory framework for covered bond programs. (published 0031 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     ======= DOW JONES NEWSWIRES ANALYSIS AND COMMENTARY ======= \par  \par EUROPEAN \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  TECHNICALS: USD STAGING CORRECTIVE RECOVERY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Intraday EUR/USD: downside consolidation is underway off Thursday's eight-month high at 1.4123, but corrective weakness is expected to be limited to the 1.3995 area. While 1.3995 holds, a test of resistance at 1.4088 and the lower peak at 1.4110 is expected, but only movement above 1.4110 would re-open the 1.4123 high. There are signs that the short-term uptrend has over-stretched and a break below 1.3995 would upgrade the setback, exposing Wednesday's low at 1.3912. (published 0605 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par EUROPEAN INTEREST RATE TECHNICALS: BONDS TO WEAKEN FURTHER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Intraday BUND: Bears are back in control of the near term following Thursday's sharp setback, and more weakness is expected to put the Oct. 1 reaction low at 130.63 at risk. Tuesday's bull trap high at 132.36 dominates the near-term, and a sustained break below 130.63 would create room for an extension lower towards the 130.00 level. Only above projected resistance at 131.61 would negate the bearish outlook, which is protected by the 131.53 high. (published 0720 GMT) [ 10-15-10 0301ET ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1030 1804 4180   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020101015e6af0004e\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
