\par\par \b \uc2 INDIAN MORNING BRIEFING: Sensex Likely To Be Rangebound\b0\par\par\uc2 1,740 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Oktober 2010\par 05:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones Energy Service\par \uc2 NRG\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par GLOBAL MARKETS \par DJIA                11094.57  -1.51   -0.01% \par Nasdaq              2435.38   -5.85   -0.24% \par S&P 500             1173.81   -4.29   -0.36% \par FTSE 100            5727.21   -20.14  -0.35% \par Nikkei Stock        9514.71   -68.80  -0.72% \par Hang Seng           23678.31  -173.86 -0.73% \par Kospi               1898.87   -0.89   -0.05% \par SGX Nifty           6195.50   +2.50   +0.04% \par Oct. contract \par  \par USD/JPY             81.44-48     -0.43% \par Range               81.84-80.90 \par EUR/USD             1.4082-89    +0.89% \par Range               1.4121-1.3956 \par  \par CBOT Wheat Dec.     $7.006 per bushel \par Comex Gold          $1,377.60    +$7.10 \par Comex Gold Range    $1,371.10-$1,388.10 \par Nymex Crude (NY)    $82.69       -$0.32 \par  \par  \par CHARTING THE SENSEX \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bombay Stock Exchange\f28 \uc2 \f2 's 30-share Sensitive Index is likely to trade in a 20,350-20,600 range, according to charts.\f28 \par \par \uc2 A shift out of this range would set the tone for the next major move. Wednesday's sharp rally followed by the completion of a bearish "key reversal day" pattern Thursday is a cause of concern. This pattern indicates the absence of follow-up buying and a lack of conviction among market participants.\par \par \uc2 A move past minor resistance at 20,600 could trigger a rise to major resistance at 20,750. But a fall below 20,350 could lead to a test of 20,250.\par \par \uc2 The National Stock Exchange's 50-share Nifty could be confined to a 6,150-6,200 band.\par \par \uc2 The Nifty has to move past Thursday's high of 6,285 to impart momentum to the uptrend. Else, a gradual drift to major support at 6,090 appears likely. A fall below Tuesday's low of 6,057 would indicate a reversal of the short-term bullish trend.\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par US STOCKS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.S. stocks closed modestly lower Thursday as investors retreated from financials because of concerns over banks' foreclosure practices.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Financials led the Dow's declines. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of America\f28 \uc2 \f2  dropped 5.2% and \f28 \uc2 \f2 J.P. Morgan Chase\f28 \uc2 \f2  fell 2.8%. Both are among the wave of banks reviewing their foreclosures after temporarily suspending evictions due to concerns over "robo signers," who approve hundreds of foreclosure documents a day. Among other banks reviewing foreclosures, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Wells Fargo\f28 \uc2 \f2  fell 5.1%.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The drop follows probes by the 50 states' attorneys general into allegations that thousands of home foreclosures were improperly handled. The flood of mortgage worries could distract from potentially positive third-quarter earnings reports expected in the next several weeks, analysts said. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Citigroup\f28 \uc2 \f2  shares fell 4.5%.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 But \f28 \uc2 \f2 Yahoo\f28 \uc2 \f2  rose 4.5% after The Wall Street Journal reported AOL and several private-equity firms, including \f28 \uc2 \f2 Silver Lake Partners\f28 \uc2 \f2  and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Blackstone Group\f28 \uc2 \f2 , are considering a possible takeover bid for the Internet company.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.S. jobs data added to jitters Thursday. The number of U.S. workers filing new claims for jobless benefits increased more than expected last week. The U.S. trade deficit also rose in August, inflated by a record-setting deficit with its largest trading partner, China.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par ASIAN STOCKS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Asian stock markets were mostly lower Friday after Wall Street's decline Thursday, with banking stocks in Seoul and Sydney weighing on those markets.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's Nikkei Stock Average, Australia's S&P/ASX 200 and South Korea's Kospi Composite were all down while New Zealand's NZX-50 was up. Dow Jones Industrial Average futures were 18 points lower in screen trade.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Tokyo market was taking a breather after Thursday's sharp rise, with exporters leading declines. The strong yen continued to remain on the forefront of investors' concerns after the U.S. dollar declined to a fresh 15-year low at Y80.88 Thursday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Canon was off 1.3%, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Sony\f28 \uc2 \f2  lost 0.7% and Sharp was down 0.5%. Among auto makers, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Honda Motor\f28 \uc2 \f2  lost 0.7% and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Toyota Motor\f28 \uc2 \f2  fell 0.9%.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Tech plays were up after shares of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Advanced Micro Devices\f28 \uc2 \f2  rose 6.5% in after-hours trade as the firm reported Thursday that its third-quarter loss narrowed on improved revenue and margins. Elpida Memory rose 2.9% and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Tokyo Electron\f28 \uc2 \f2  tacked on 2.4%.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Banking stocks in Korea and Australian were down as they reacted to concerns on Wall Street over banks' foreclosure practices. In Sydney, ANZ bank lost 1.0% and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Westpac\f28 \uc2 \f2  bank was off 0.9%, while in Seoul, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Woori Finance\f28 \uc2 \f2  fell 1.3% and KB Financial dropped 1.1%.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In South Korea, insurance plays were down after the Bank of Korea's decision to leave its key rate unchanged Thursday as brokers said a rate hike would have boosted their earnings outlook. Samsung Fire & Marine lost 1.7% and Korea Life was off 0.5%.\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 The euro was at $1.4028 against the dollar, from $1.4077 late Thursday in New York, and at Y114.47 against the yen, from Y114.74. The dollar was buying Y81.56, from Y81.51.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par METALS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Gold futures printed a fresh record settlement Thursday as monetary tightening in Singapore sent investors out of the U.S. dollar and into the perceived hedge of the metal. Spot gold was down $3.00 at $1,378.20 per troy ounce from the New York close Thursday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Base metals closed mixed on the London Metal Exchange Thursday after toppling from multi-month highs in jittery trade as U.S. labor figures disappointed.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par OIL SUMMARY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Crude oil futures retreated from early gains Thursday in U.S. trading, settling lower as a government report showed U.S. demand for petroleum products fell to the lowest level in nearly a year. November Nymex crude oil futures took a breather after rising to a five-session high at $84.12 per barrel Thursday. The contract was down 4 cents at $82.65 on Globex.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par CALENDAR OF EVENTS Oct. 15 \par 1115 IST New Delhi:   Oil minister, federal oil secretary, upstream \par                       regulator head at press meeting on oil, gas \par                       block auctions \par 1200 IST Mumbai:      White House National Economic Council director, \par                       \f28 \uc2 \f2 Kotak Mahindra Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  chairman at event \par 1200 IST Mumbai:      \f28 \uc2 \f2 State Bank of India\f28 \uc2 \f2  chairman at press meeting \par                       to discuss forthcoming bond issue \par 1200 IST Chandigarh:  Reserve bank of India governor, deputy \par                       governors at press meeting after \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  \par                       board meeting \par 1200 IST New Delhi:   Wholesale price index data for September \par 1230 IST Bangalore:   \f28 \uc2 \f2 Infosys Technologies\f28 \uc2 \f2  executives at 2Q earnings \par                       press meeting \par EARNINGS:             \f28 \uc2 \f2 Development Credit Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2 , \f28 \uc2 \f2 HeidelbergCement\f28 \uc2 \f2  \par                       India, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Karnataka Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  \par 0900 GMT EU:          August foreign trade \par 0900 GMT EU:          September Harmonized consumer price index \par 1215 GMT US:          Federal Reserve chairman speech \par 1230 GMT US:          October Empire State manufacturing survey \par 1230 GMT US:          September advance monthly sales for retail and \par                       food services \par 1230 GMT US:          September consumer price index \par 1355 GMT US:          October Thomson Reuters/University of Michigan \par                       Survey of Consumers - preliminary \par 1400 GMT US:          August manufacturing and trade: inventories and \par                       sales \par  \par  \par TOP HEADLINES - Dow Jones/WSJ \par =UPDATE: \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  FINANCE MINISTER CONTINUES \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  TALK \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's finance minister kept the possibility of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market on the table Friday, saying the government will take "decisive" steps if necessary, after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  touched a 15-year high of Y80.88 to the dollar overnight. (published 0125 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BOJ GOVERNOR: READY TO TAKE APPROPRIATE POLICY STEPS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bank of Japan Gov. Masaaki Shirakawa said Friday that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is ready to take appropriate monetary policy measures amid downside risks to the domestic economy such as the rising yen and slowing overseas economies. (published 0048 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par S KOREA FIN MIN: \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCY\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  TENSIONS GROWING, SEE SIGNS OF PROTECTIONISM \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korea's Minister of Strategy and Finance Yoon Jeung-hyun said Friday that tensions among advanced and emerging economies over \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rates are growing, and may result in countries setting up trade barriers. (published 0200 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA'S SEPTEMBER URBAN PROPERTY PRICES UP 0.5% VS AUGUST \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Property prices in 70 of China's large and medium-sized cities rose 0.5% in September from the previous month, and were up 9.1% from a year earlier, the National Bureau of Statistics said Friday. (published 0041 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PBOC ZHOU: TO CONTINUE TO MANAGE YUAN EXCHANGE RATE BASED ON EXISTING TRADING BAND - REPORT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China will continue to manage the yuan's exchange rate based on the existing trading band to maintain the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's basic stability, People's Bank of China Gov. Zhou Xiaochuan wrote in an article in the PBOC-backed magazine China Finance on Friday. (published 0050 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: FED'S KOCHERLAKOTA: NEW FED ASSET PURCHASES WOULD HAVE 'MORE MUTED' IMPACT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A fresh round of asset purchases to stimulate a sagging economy might not help as much as some hope, the president of the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Federal Reserve Bank of Minneapolis\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Thursday. (published 2229 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par DOOSAN MECATEC RAISES KRW264.3 BLN VIA DOOSAN INFRACORE BLOCK SALE - SOURCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korean plant builder Doosan Mecatec has raised KRW264.3 billion by selling a 6.03% stake in \f28 \uc2 \f2 Doosan Infracore Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . via a block sale, a person familiar with the situation said Friday. (published 0057 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =GRAND JURY INDICTS FORMER CHI MEI EXEC IN LCD PRICE-FIX PROBE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A federal grand jury indicted a former Taiwan executive as part of a ongoing antitrust investigation into price fixing on liquid-crystal display panels, the ninth such indictment in the case so far. (published 2320 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =2ND UPDATE: AMD 3Q LOSS NARROWS ON HIGHER SALES; SEES FLAT 4Q REV \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Advanced Micro Devices Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 . posted a 16% rise in third-quarter revenue as weak consumer demand for personal computers didn't take as large a toll as feared. (published 2227 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =2ND UPDATE: SEAGATE EVALUATES SUGGESTION IT GO PRIVATE AGAIN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 10-14-10 2300ET ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Seagate Technology PLC\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Thursday it has been approached by an unnamed party interested in taking the storage drive maker private, a move that comes as interest in the broad data management sector heats up. (published 0000 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par TOP HEADLINES - Indian Media \par India's GMR, JSW Enter Non-binding Bids For Canada's CIC Energy - Business Standard \par India's \f28 \uc2 \f2 Tara Jewels\f28 \uc2 \f2  To Raise INR2 Bln Via Initial Public Offer - PTI \par India's Hydrocarbons Agency Delays Clearing Reliance Industries KGD6 Expenses - Livemint.com \par Bharti Enterprises In Talks With Bank Of India To Sell Bharti AXA Stake - Economic Times \par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bharti Airtel\f28 \uc2 \f2  To Outsource Customer Support For African \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  - Economic Times \par India's ONGC May Partner Winning Bidder For Russian Opil Fields - Economic Times \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 10-14-10 2300ET ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 62500   \par \par \uc2 Dokument NRG0000020101015e6af00007\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
