\par\par \b \uc2 CORRECTED-S.Korea c.bank head: Japan min comment inappropriate\b0\par\par\uc2 160 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Oktober 2010\par 05:22\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Adds dropped word to lead paragraph to show \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief said comments were not appropriate)\par \par \uc2 SEOUL, Oct 14 (Reuters) - South Korea's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  head said on Thursday that discussing another country's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy is not appropriate, when asked about remarks by \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's finance minister on South Korea's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "It is inappropriate to talk about a certain country's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy unilaterally," Bank of Korea Governor Kim Choong-soo told reporters at a news conference.\par \par \uc2 Japanese Finance Minister Yoshihiko Noda said on Wednesday that South Korea's leadership of the G20 could be called into question because of Seoul's regular \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem the won's <KRW=> rise. (Reporting by Kim Yeon-hee; Editing by Chris Lewis)\par \par \uc2 BOK/\b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  (URGENT, CORRECTED)|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|O|OIL|C|GRO|MTL|SOF|J|ABX|RNP|DNP|PCM|PEN   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020101014e6ae0005c\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
