\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar drops to 2010 low vs major rivals\b0\par\par\uc2 906 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Oktober 2010\par 02:57\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Singapore widens trading band for Singapore dollar\par \par \uc2 * Euro rises above $1.4100, highest in more than 8 months\par \par \uc2 * Aussie flirts with parity, dollar index hits 2010 low (Updates prices)\par \par \uc2 NEW YORK, Oct 14 (Reuters) - The U.S. dollar slid to a 2010 low against a basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Thursday after Singapore let its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rise but analysts saw increasing chances of a dollar rebound with negative sentiment so high.\par \par \uc2 The Australian dollar, which boasts the highest yield among major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , soared to its strongest since the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was floated in 1983 as investors dumped the U.S. dollar on expectations the Federal Reserve would start printing money through further quantitative easing as soon as next month.\par \par \uc2 Singapore's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  widened the trading band in which it maintains the Singapore dollar <SGD=> <SGD=D4>, propelling it to a record high. Singapore is experiencing rising inflation and the move was seen as a tightening of policy -- the opposite of what the U.S. Federal Reserve is expected to do.\par \par \uc2 The Chinese yuan <CNY=CFXS> hit its highest close against the U.S. dollar since July 2005. For more see [ID:nSGE69D09L].\par \par \uc2 "Singapore is often seen as a bellwether for the rest of the Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Firas Askari, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading at BMO Capital Markets in Toronto. "It opens the way for the region to have \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  gains (against the U.S. dollar)."\par \par \uc2 The dollar index <.DXY>, which tumbled to its weakest since December, is on course to test trendline support at 75.95, with its November low of 74.17 then not far away. The 75.95 target is the trendline from two major lows in July 2008 and in November 2009. CMC Markets places support after 74.17 at 70.70, the low from March 2008.\par \par \uc2 The dollar index was last down 0.6 percent at 76.593.\par \par \uc2 The euro <EUR=> surged to a more than eight-month high of $1.4123 on trading platform EBS <EUR=EBS> and faces near-term resistance at $1.4195, the Jan. 25 high. Traders said the euro still has room to go, with strong resistance not seen until $1.45. The pair was last at $1.4067, up 0.8 percent.\par \par \uc2 After the euro failed to crack $1.40 the previous session, the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's moves caught some players by surprise as they had been expecting more consolidation. It triggered stops around $1.4030 and then $1.4050 in Asia and subsequently cracked the $1.41 handle in Europe.\par \par \uc2 While a short-term consolidation may still be on the cards, CitiFX says it still sees the pair making a run at $1.4360-70 and then $1.4720.\par \par \uc2 The Aussie dollar last traded at US$0.9935 <AUD=>, up 0.3 percent, with traders saying option barriers at $1.0000 were slowing the rally. It has gained about 11 percent this year and is up more than 20 percent from a low in May.\par \par \uc2 The options market suggests the recent upward momentum in the Aussie dollar has further to run. [ID:nLDE69711U]\par \par \uc2 DOLLAR BOUNCE?\par \par \uc2 Dollar selling accelerated after the release of Federal Reserve meeting minutes this week showing policy makers were considering more measures to stimulate the economy, including adopting a price-level target or buying more bonds.\par \par \uc2 Investors will closely watch a speech by Fed Chairman Ben Bernanke on Friday which could provide hints on what the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  might do at its next policy meeting on Nov. 2-3.\par \par \uc2 Lee Hardman, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  economist at \uc2 The Bank of Tokyo-Mitsubishi UFJ\uc2  in London, said dollar pessimism, judged by many metrics, is now at "historically extreme levels signaling an elevated risk of a sharp correction higher for the dollar when dollar selling has reached a crescendo."\par \par \uc2 "At the end of the day, when everybody is on the boat and everybody is doing the same ..., it doesn't take much to make the boat go the other way," BMO Capital's Askari said.\par \par \uc2 The dollar could see a rebound if the Fed announces asset purchases of less than $1 trillion after its meeting in November, which would disappoint some market participants hoping for a bigger move and ease concerns about a debasement of the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Jack Spitz, managing director of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  at \uc2 National Bank of Canada\uc2  in Toronto, said with the market already pricing in Fed easing, the dollar could rise after the Fed meeting in a "sell the rumor, buy the fact" reaction.\par \par \uc2 The dollar also hit the latest in a succession of record lows against the Swiss franc <CHF=> and slid below parity with the Canadian dollar <CAD=>, a level not seen since April.\par \par \uc2 The greenback fell to a 15-year low of 80.88 yen <JPY=> on EBS, despite wariness about Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and looked set to challenge its record low of 79.75 hit in April 1995.\par \par \uc2 While traders think the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  could \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  at any moment to keep the yen in check, some market participants speculated that Tokyo may prefer to avoid \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  ahead of G20 meetings in South Korea in October and November. (Reporting by Nick Olivari and Wanfeng Zhou; Additional reporting by Neal Armstrong in London; Editing by James Dalgleish)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 9)|LANGEN|C|D|E|M|O|U|MTL|GRO|SOF|OIL|UKI|CANT|AUF|J|Z|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020101014e6ae0001p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
