wed as unsurprising; also report says the loans identified as risky amount to 4% of China's total outstanding loans, government has funds to support lenders. Shanghai Composite Index +0.4% at 2873.84, off intraday high at 2919.41; tipped to trade around 2850-2900 level for remainder of session. "Money that has been restricted from investing in to property (due to recent tightening measures) is going into the stock market, so the ample liquidity will support the index for awhile," says Amy Lin from Capital Securities. \uc2 China Merchants Bank\uc2  (600036.SH) +2.1% at CNY14.80, Bank of China (601988.SH) +1.5% at CNY3.50. Shenzhen Composite Index down 1.4% at 1212.42. (esther.fung@dowjones.com) [ 10-14-10 0034ET ]\par \par \uc2 4022   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020101014e6ae0003p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
