\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK: Gold/Silver Ratio Could Bounce - Trader\b0\par\par\uc2 1,643 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Oktober 2010\par 05:11\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in Singapore. 65 64154 140; \par MarketTalk@dowjones.com \par  \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 0311 GMT [Dow Jones] Spot silver at $24.29/oz, just off 30-year high at $24.37; has rallied 37% since August 24 when it broke out of previous range; gold/silver ratio has dropped from 69 to today's 56.5 in that time and could be due for some kind of reversal, says Mark van der Sluys, managing director at Bullionmark in Sydney. "Silver is being driven by new money coming into the market. There is investment money but there's also speculative cash chasing this." Adds could be worth buying gold/silver ratio as any correction/consolidation phase in precious metals almost certain to see gold outperform. Adds can't rule out more gains for gold, silver with shallowness of any dips testament to amount of new money seeking exposure to precious metals. "Even experienced traders are no longer waiting for a correction, they are seeing any sign of stability as a chance to accumulate a larger position." (james.campbell@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0308 GMT [Dow Jones] NZX-50 +0.8% as risk appetite remains strong, with strong gains in regional markets supporting sentiment, says \uc2 Craigs Investment Partners\uc2  broker Belinda Stanley; "Offshore is anticipating a good earnings week coming from stocks in U.S. It started off relatively well so people are feeling rather buoyant even with the lukewarm economic data coming out both offshore and here." Says good sentiment helping heavyweights; Fletcher Building (FBU.NZ) +1.4% at NZ$8.30, Telecom NZ (TEL.NZ) +2.5% at NZ$2.07, \uc2 Contact Energy\uc2  (CEN.NZ) +0.4% at NZ$5.68. NZX-50 last 3257.30. (lucy.craymer@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0306 GM