\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK: USD/JPY Hits Fresh 15-Yr Low;Support At 81-Dealer\b0\par\par\uc2 1,566 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Oktober 2010\par 04:42\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in Singapore. 65 64154 140; \par MarketTalk@dowjones.com \par  \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0242 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/JPY hits fresh 15-year low at 81.28 as broad-based USD weakness, exacerbated earlier by Singapore \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  monetary tightening, continues to weigh on pair. But investors' continued caution over possible JPY-selling \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  authorities may keep pair supported above 81.00 for rest of global day, says Satoshi Okagawa, senior \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dealer at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Sumitomo Mitsui Banking Corporation\f28 \uc2 \f2 . Says strong Asian share markets may also offer support as JPY loses safe-haven sheen. For these reasons, says "it wouldn't be strange if we start seeing more bids on the dollar-yen now." Pair last at 81.32. (andrew.monahan@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 0240 GMT [Dow Jones] China shares extend gains, led by banks after a bad loans investigation by regulators indicated nothing new, analysts say. Shanghai Composite Index +1.7% at 2910.62, faces immediate resistance at 2950. "Banks are leading because they already pre-digested risks from bad loans to local governments. Today after the report came out, the loan risks are more certain and there appears to be no other risks to worry about," says Zhang Zhuo at Minsheng Securities. \uc2 China Merchants Bank\uc2  (600036.SH) +3.7% at CNY15.02, Bank of China (601988.SH) +2.3% at CNY3.53. Shenzhen Composite Index flat at 1229.48. (esther.fung@dowjones.com)\par 