\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Rise on Fed view; won up on Japan finmin\b0\par\par\uc2 758 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Oktober 2010\par 05:41\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited    \par \par \uc2 * Won up 1 pct on \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's comments on S.Korea \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 * Baht at 13-yr high despite tax plan; c.bank spotted\par \par \uc2 * Caution over measures to check \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strength remain\par \par \uc2 By Cheon Jong-woo\par \par \uc2 SEOUL, Oct 13 (Reuters) - The South Korean won led gains in Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the dollar on Wednesday after Federal Reserve minutes supported expectations of further quantitative easing.\par \par \uc2 The won found further support after Japanese Finance Minister Yoshihiko Noda said South Korea's leadership of the Group of 20 nations forum could come under question because of its regular \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . [ID:nTOE69C00G]\par \par \uc2 The comments prompted some expectations that Seoul's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  authorities may scale back dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but investors remained cautious that the country may still take other steps to check the won's strength, analysts and dealers said.\par \par \uc2 "Dollar purchases, which have been ineffective, are not the only way. As we saw from Thailand yesterday, Asian countries will look for regulations, which are a global trend," said Jeong My-young, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 Samsung Futures Inc\uc2  in Seoul.\par \par \uc2 The regional authorities were estimated to have bought a combined $32.7 billion via \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  between Sept 27 and Oct 12, according to traders' estimates compiled by IFR Markets. [ID:nSGE69C059]\par \par \uc2 Thailand's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  were spotted \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  as the Baht hit a fresh 13-year high despite the country's taxation plan, dealers said. Malaysia's authorities were seen stepping in the market.\par \par \uc2 Central banks of Thailand and Malaysia were spotted buying dollars for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said.\par \par \uc2 WON\par \par \uc2 The won <KRW=> rose 1 percent as Noda's comments and expectations for the Fed's further easing prompted investors to clear dollar long positions.\par \par \uc2 The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  ended domestic trade at 1,120.7 from Tuesday's domestic close <KRW=KFTC> of 1,131.5.\par \par \uc2 Despite Noda's remarks and expectations of further rises, investors remained wary of the authorities' measures to cap the won's strength.\par \par \uc2 "Nobody questions on the won's bullish trend, but few are confident whether the won can breaks through 1,100. It is difficult to chase it more aggressively around this level," said a local bank dealer in Seoul.\par \par \uc2 TAIWAN DOLLAR\par \par \uc2 The Taiwan dollar <TWD=TP> rose nearly 1 percent, moving in towards a more-than-two-year high hit last week, after the Fed hinted at more quantitative easing in the world No.1 economy.\par \par \uc2 It rose to as high as T$30.78 against the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the first minutes of trade, compared with Tuesday's close of T$31.07 when the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was suspected of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 BAHT\par \par \uc2 The Thai baht <THB=> hit a 13-year high of 29.73 per dollar, extending gains a day after the Thai government announced a 15 percent withholding tax on profits made by foreign investors on Thai bonds [ID:nSGE69B0A6].\par \par \uc2 Traders earlier detected sporadic \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \uc2 Bank of Thailand\uc2  after the baht tested 29.83-85 per dollar.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR Change on the day at 0700 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen        81.91          81.76       -0.18\par  Sing dlr        1.3054         1.3056       +0.02\par  Taiwan dlr      30.875         31.070       +0.63\par  Korean won     1119.65        1131.50       +1.06\par  Baht             29.79          29.98       +0.64\par  Peso             43.47          43.64       +0.39\par  Rupiah         8922.00        8937.00       +0.17\par  Rupee            44.48          44.66       +0.40\par  Ringgit         3.0980         3.1070       +0.29\par  Yuan            6.6720         6.6734       +0.02\par  Change so far in 2010\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen        81.91          92.90      +13.42\par  Sing dlr        1.3054         1.4053       +7.65\par  Taiwan dlr      30.875         32.030       +3.74\par  Korean won     1119.65        1164.50       +4.01\par  Baht             29.79          33.32      +11.85\par  Peso             43.47          46.20       +6.28\par  Rupiah         8922.00        9420.00       +5.58\par  Rupee            44.48          46.54       +4.63\par  Ringgit         3.0980         3.4220      +10.46\par  Yuan            6.6720         6.8270       +2.32\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Additional reporting by Vithoon Amorn in Bangkok and Ralph Jennings in TAIPEI, Clement Tan in Singapore and Catherine Tan at IFR Markets; Editing by Kazunori Takada)\f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-ASIA-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|D|E|RBN|IF|PHD|S