s regarding (\b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  (into the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market) is hard to obtain," says Yutaka Miura, senior technical analyst at Mizuho Securities. "Investors are still watching for an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  move, but the wariness is beginning to fade." Resource-linked shares likely to outperform on gains in gold and crude futures. Nikkei 225 December futures ended Chicago trading at 9500 vs Osaka close at 9410. (kana.inagaki@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 2300 GMT [Dow Jones] PREVIEW: Views sharply divided over whether BOK will resume monetary tightening Thursday by raising policy rate after defying expectations for rate hike at 2 previous meetings; 9 of 17 economists, fixed-income analysts surveyed by Dow Jones expect BOK to hike key rate by 25 bps to 2.50%; balance 8 tip on-hold decision (with 4 of these predicting 25 bps hike before year-out, rest forecast no move until 1Q 2011). "Judging from economic fundamentals, the BOK should resume rate hikes after having paused for two months," says DBS Group in research note. But given latest capital inflows into Asia due to further quantitative easing in Japan, expectations Fed will follow soon, BOK likely to be "reluctant" to hike at this point as higher rates would invite more inflows and further pressure KRW higher, it adds. Rate decision due around 0100 GMT Thursday. (In-Soo.Nam@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 2300 GMT [Dow Jones] PREVIEW: Views sharply divided over whether BOK will resume monetary tightening Thursday by raising policy rate after defying expectations for rate hike at 2 previous meetings; 9 of 17 economists, fixed-income analysts surveyed by Dow Jones expect BOK to hike key rate by 25 bps to 2.50%; balance 8 tip on-hold decision (with 4 of these predicting 25 bps hike before year-out, rest forecast no move until 1Q 2011). "Judging from economic fundamental