\par\par \b \uc2 Japan Finance Minister: To Take Decisive Action On  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  If Needed\b0\par\par\uc2 178 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Oktober 2010\par 02:22\par \uc2 Dow Jones Business News\par \uc2 DJON\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 TOKYO -(Dow Jones)- Japan's finance minister reiterated Tuesday that the government would take "decisive" action, including \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , if necessary to stem the yen's rise.\par \par \uc2 "I explained to the G-7 that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's previous \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was aimed at curbing excessive appreciation in the yen that could hurt the Japanese economy," Yoshihiko Noda said at his first press conference since returning from a meeting of finance ministers and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials of the Group of Seven industrialized nations.\par \par \uc2 The remarks came after the dollar fell to a 15-year low of Y81.37 against the yen Monday. At 0000 GMT Tuesday, the dollar was at Y82.29.\par \par \uc2 "G-7 members reconfirmed that volatile \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market moves have a negative impact on the economy and financial markets," Noda said.\par \par \uc2 He added that the Japanese government will watch \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market moves "with great interest."\par \par \uc2 -By Tomoyuki Tachikawa, Dow Jones Newswires; +81-3-6269-2787; tomoyuki.tachikawa@dowjones.com [ 10-11-10 2022ET ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJON000020101012e6ac00002\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
