\par\par \b \uc2 WORLD  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 : Yen Rises Vs Dollar Despite Japan Government Warnings\b0\par\par\uc2 By Takashi Mochizuki   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 511 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Oktober 2010\par 07:44\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--The yen rose against the dollar in Asia Tuesday despite warnings of possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the Japanese government, as investors viewed any action by Tokyo as not powerful enough to change the direction of the market.\par \par \uc2 Finance Minister Yoshihiko Noda reiterated earlier in the day that the government would take "decisive steps", including \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , if necessary to stem the yen's rise.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, amid speculation that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's stance on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  may find a lack of support among other leading economies, Economy Minister Banri Kaieda said that Noda explained Tokyo's view at a weekend meeting of financial chiefs from the Group of Seven industrialized nations in Washington and "seemed to get some understanding from his counterparts."\par \par \uc2 But investors shrugged off the remarks and increased their holdings of the yen. At 0450 GMT the dollar was at Y81.94, down from Y82.13 in New York Monday. Dealers said it's only a matter of time before the greenback drops below Y81.00.\par \par \uc2 Funds have been selling the greenback for the yen on the view that the U.S. Federal Reserve is likely to ease its monetary policy further in early November.\par \par \uc2 "Japan is likely to step into the market again if the dollar continues to drop toward Y80.00, but it can't do it in a very aggressive manner, meaning the effects will be very limited," said Shinichi Hayashi, a senior dealer at \uc2 Shinkin \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Elsewhere, the euro fell to Y113.58 and $1.3862 from Y113.97 and $1.3877 as investors turned away from riskier \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  due to weaker Japanese equities. At 0530 GMT, the Nikkei Stock Average was down 1.9%.\par \par \uc2 The ICE Dollar Index, which tracks the greenback against a trade-weighted basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , was at 77.518 from 77.500.\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Interbank \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Foreign Exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Rates At 00:50 EDT / 0450 GMT \par  \par                          Latest     Previous   %Chg   Daily   Daily    %Chg \par Dollar Rates                        2150 GMT          High    Low      12/31 \par  \par USD/JPY Yen              81.90-95   82.11-15   -0.26  82.34   81.86   -12.01 \par EUR/USD Euro             1.3860-67  1.3876-79  -0.12  1.3886  1.3846   -3.19 \par GBP/USD Sterling         1.5893-96  1.5877-82  +0.10  1.5913  1.5870   -1.67 \par USD/CHF Swiss Franc      0.9640-50  0.9644-49  -0.04  0.9660  0.9640   -6.90 \par USD/CAD Canadian Dlr     1.0143-48  1.0138-39  +0.05  1.0148  1.0130   -3.52 \par AUD/USD Australian Dlr   0.9787-92  0.9840-41  -0.54  0.9841  0.9783   +8.95 \par NZD/USD New Zealand Dlr  0.7492-02  0.7517-27  -0.33  0.7526  0.7484   +3.25 \par EUR/JPY Yen              113.55-60  113.96-01  -0.36  114.15  113.57  -14.79 \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Takashi Mochizuki, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-6269-2782; takashi.mochizuki@dowjones.com [ 12-10-10 0544GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1034 1863 28038 4162   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020101012e6ac000bz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
