\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 693 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Oktober 2010\par 07:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par JAPAN FINANCE MINISTER: TO TAKE DECISIVE ACTION ON \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  IF NEEDED \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's finance minister reiterated Tuesday that the government would take "decisive" action, including \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , if necessary to stem the yen's rise. (publ ished 0007 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par JAPAN ECONOMY MINISTER: G-7 SHOWED 'UNDERSTANDING' ON ACTION VS YEN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's economy minister said Tuesday that his colleague, the finance minister, reported that officials from the Group of Seven industrialized nations showed understanding about \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market in September. (published 0019 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =UPDATE: CHINA SAFE REVISES UP CURRENT ACCOUNT, WARNS ABOUT INFLOWS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  regulator on Tuesday revised slightly upwards its estimates of the country's current account surplus--the broadest measure of its trade balance--in the second quarter and first half, and warned that destabilizing hot money inflows are set to continue in the second half. (published 0410 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par AUSTRALIA SEPTEMBER BUSINESS CONDITIONS UP 2 POINTS TO +7-NAB SURVEY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australian business conditions rose slightly in September while confidence slipped but the economy continues to exhibit a two-speed pattern, with conditions for mining and transport outstripping retail and manufacturing, according to a survey released Tuesday. (published 0030 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =UPDATE: AUSTRALIA'S PM SAYS GLOBAL CONDITIONS STILL UNCERTAIN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The global economy is recovering but conditions in the global financial system could still jump from benign to crisis-mode "very rapidly", Australia's Prime Minister Julia Gillard said Tuesday. (published 0432 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =UPDATE: CHINA PAPER: '\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCY\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  WAR' MAY CAUSE BUBBLES, INFLATION \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Quantitative easing in the U.S. and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by various countries to limit the rise of their \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , a situation many have likened to a "\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  war," could create a new wave of global asset bubbles and inflation, the China Securities Journal argued Tuesday in a front-page editorial. (published 0433 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par SOUTH KOREA: FINANCIAL SECTOR ASSET QUALITY BROADLY WEAKER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korean financial watchdog Financial Supervisory Service said Tuesday that the asset quality of domestic financial sector players have generally weakened due in part to their exposure to nationwide corporate restructuring efforts. (published 0100 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par NEW ZEALAND'S ECONOMIC RECOVERY REMAINS SLOW, FRAGILE - RBNZ \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Reserve Bank of New Zealand reiterated Tuesday the country's economic recovery remains slow and fragile, as could be expected given the economic recession coincided with a financial crisis. (published 2232 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =UPDATE: PHILIPPINE EXPORTS RISE TO RECORD VALUE IN AUGUST \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Philippine exports surged to a record high in August, rising 37% from a year earlier due to stronger shipments of petroleum products, electronics, coconut oil and metal components. (published 0414 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =UPDATE: \f28 \uc2 \f2 BANK OF THAILAND\f28 \uc2 \f2  TO FOCUS ON PRICE, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  STABILITY -OFFICIAL \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Monetary authorities in Thailand are aiming for the orderly adjustment of exchange rates and price stability amid a surge of capital inflows, a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  official said Tuesday, highlighting the problems facing Asian economies due to a glut of liquidity and low interest rates in developed countries. (published 0344 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =DATA SNAP: UK HOUSE PRICES FALL FURTHER IN SEPTEMBER -RICS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.K. residential property prices slipped further in September as a fresh influx of homes for sale combined with a lack of buyers, the Royal Institution of Chartered Surveyors said Tuesday. (published 2301 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =DATA SNAP: UK RETAIL SALES GROWTH SLOWED IN SEPT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.K. retail sales growth slowed in September, with higher food prices accounting for most of the increase since the same month last year, according to a monthly survey by the British Retail Consortium. (published 2301 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UK 3Q ECON GROWTH EASED, GOVT, MPC MUST SUPPORT PRIVATE SECTOR-BCC \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The British Chambers of Commerce called for action from the government and the Bank of England to ward off a double-dip recession after its latest survey showed economic activity eased in the third quarter. (published 2301 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ======= DOW JONES NEWSWIRES ANALYSIS AND COMMENTARY ======= \par  \par =CHARTING ASIA: EURO MAY FALL TO $1.3478 IN COMING DAYS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The euro may continue its retreat in coming days after pulling back from a brief run to near a multimonth high over $1.40, technical charts suggest. (published 0202 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 12-10-10 0500GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1030 1804 4180   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020101012e6ac000a5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
