ned due in part to their exposure to nationwide corporate restructuring efforts. (published 0100 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par NEW ZEALAND'S ECONOMIC RECOVERY REMAINS SLOW, FRAGILE - RBNZ \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Reserve Bank of New Zealand reiterated Tuesday the country's economic recovery remains slow and fragile, as could be expected given the economic recession coincided with a financial crisis. (published 2232 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =DATA SNAP: PHILIPPINE EXPORTS AT RECORD HIGH $4.74 BLN IN AUGUST \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Philippine exports continued to gathered pace in August, rising 37% from a year earlier to the highest ever for a single month due to a strong surge in shipments of petroleum products, electronics, coconut oil and metal components. (published 0123 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par THAI \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CENTRAL BANK\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  EXECUTIVE: MONETARY POLICY WILL FOCUS ON PRICE STABILITY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Amid excessive capital inflows to Asia stemming from a glut of liquidity globally, monetary authorities in Thailand are aiming for orderly adjustment of exchange rates and price stability, an official from the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Thailand\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Tuesday. (published 0154 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =DATA SNAP: UK HOUSE PRICES FALL FURTHER IN SEPTEMBER -RICS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.K. residential property prices slipped further in September as a fresh influx of homes for sale combined with a lack of buyers, the Royal Institution of Chartered Surveyors said Tuesday. (published 2301 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =DATA SNAP: UK RETAIL SALES GROWTH SLOWED IN SEPT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.K. retail sales growth slowed in September, with higher food prices accounting for most of the increase since the same month last year, according to a monthly survey by the British Retail Consortium. (published 2301 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2