\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 415 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Oktober 2010\par 03:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par JAPAN FINANCE MINISTER: TO TAKE DECISIVE ACTION ON \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  IF NEEDED \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's finance minister reiterated Tuesday that the government would take "decisive" action, including \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , if necessary to stem the yen's rise. (published 0007 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par JAPAN ECONOMY MINISTER: G-7 SHOWED 'UNDERSTANDING' ON ACTION VS YEN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's economy minister said Tuesday that his colleague, the finance minister, reported that officials from the Group of Seven industrialized nations showed understanding about \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market in September. (published 0019 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par AUSTRALIA SEPTEMBER BUSINESS CONDITIONS UP 2 POINTS TO +7-NAB SURVEY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australian business conditions rose slightly in September while confidence slipped but the economy continues to exhibit a two-speed pattern, with conditions for mining and transport outstripping retail and manufacturing, according to a survey released Tuesday. (published 0030 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par SOUTH KOREA: FINANCIAL SECTOR ASSET QUALITY BROADLY WEAKER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korean financial watchdog Financial Supervisory Service said Tuesday that the asset quality of domestic financial sector players have generally weakened due in part to their exposure to nationwide corporate restructuring efforts. (published 0100 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par NEW ZEALAND'S ECONOMIC RECOVERY REMAINS SLOW, FRAGILE - RBNZ \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Reserve Bank of New Zealand reiterated Tuesday the country's economic recovery remains slow and fragile, as could be expected given the economic recession coincided with a financial crisis. (published 2232 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =ECB'S NOWOTNY: NO INFLATION OR DEFLATION IN EURO ZONE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 There are currently no signs of inflation in the U.S. or euro zone, European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Governing Council member Ewald Nowotny said Monday. (published 2247 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =DATA SNAP: UK HOUSE PRICES FALL FURTHER IN SEPTEMBER -RICS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.K. residential property prices slipped further in September as a fresh influx of homes for sale combined with a lack of buyers, the Royal Institution of Chartered Surveyors said Tuesday. (published 2301 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =DATA SNAP: UK RETAIL SALES GROWTH SLOWED IN SEPT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.K. retail sales growth slowed in September, with higher food prices accounting for most of the increase since the same month last year, according to a monthly survey by the British Retail Consortium. (published 2301 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UK 3Q ECON GROWTH EASED, GOVT, MPC MUST SUPPORT PRIVATE SECTOR-BCC \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The British Chambers of Commerce called for action from the government and the Bank of England to ward off a double-dip recession after its latest survey showed economic activity eased in the third quarter. (published 2301 GMT) [ 12-10-10 0100GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1030 1804 4180   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020101012e6ac0001z\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscale